  bd450e6adcc9a971 t("A conversation is not one task, so ×N runs says nothing there. What matters: how long it has been waiting for you, how long the current run is in work, who works it, and a start that keeps failing. The bare last-activity age gives way to the time that matters for the row's state; the now line stays. Long waits and long runs stand out against the other rows of the same group (peerFence), never against a fixed number. Time is always the rightmost fact (owner, 25 Nov): ×N, then the agent mark, then the time, so times line up in one column down the list. ",Inter:$font.family,13:$font.size.md,r,align(l),lh(auto,1.23)) p(32,83) s(1240,hug:48) f[(94df5300066a67b0,tok(fleet.fg-muted,#9A9A9F))] "note"
